[s2;= Tutorial: U`+`+ Box&]
[s5;%- While modern 3D model renderers or game engines rely heavily 
on hardware`-accelerated APIs like OpenGL or Vulkan, understanding 
the fundamentals of 3D graphics often begins with software rasterization. 
With [C^topic`:`/`/Sculptor`/src`/Upp`_Sculptor`_en`-us`#Upp`:`:Sculptor^ Sculptor],
 you can render fully textured, lit, and transformed 3D geometry 
entirely on the CPU using a lightweight software rasterizer designed 
specifically for the U`+`+ development framework.&]
[s5;%- In this tutorial, we will explore [C^topic`:`/`/Sculptor`/src`/Upp`_Sculptor`_en`-us`#Upp`:`:Sculptor^ S
culptor]`'s CPU`-based architecture, examine how textures and 
geometry are managed on the host side, and assemble a complete 
U`+`+ application featuring a rotating, lit 3D cube.&]
