[s3;:1: 1. Sculptor`'s Architecture&]
[s5; Before diving into code, it is important to understand how Sculptor 
operates compared to traditional GPU wrappers:&]
[s22;:1`.1: 1.1. CPU`-based Software Rasterization&]
[s5; Unlike frameworks that interface directly with OS`-level GPU 
contexts and external shader programs, a software renderer such 
as [^topic`:`/`/Sculptor`/src`/Upp`_Sculptor`_en`-us`#Upp`:`:Sculptor^ Sculptor 
]computes all geometry clipping, perspective projection, triangle 
setup, and texturing directly on the host CPU. This architecture 
eliminates the need for graphics context initialization boilerplate, 
making it ideal for lightweight utility windows, offline rendering 
tools, or educational applications where hardware acceleration 
is either unavailable or unnecessary.&]
[s22;:1`.2: 1.2. The Canvas and Frame Buffer Management&]
[s5;%- Software rendering requires an allocated memory space to act 
as a digital canvas. [%%^topic`:`/`/Sculptor`/src`/Upp`_Sculptor`_en`-us`#Upp`:`:Sculptor^ S
culptor ]engine manages this by creating an internal pixel color 
buffer and a depth (Z) buffer sized dynamically to match the 
host window. Throughout a rendering pass, individual triangles 
are rasterized pixel`-by`-pixel into this memory space. Once 
rasterization completes, the buffer is packaged into a standard 
GUI image object ready for immediate blitting onto the UI canvas.&]
[s22;:1`.3:%- 1.3.Matrix Stack and Transformations&]
[s5;%- Similar to fixed`-function graphics pipelines, the engine 
maintains an internal matrix stack to handle spatial transformations. 
Operations such as [^topic`:`/`/Sculptor`/src`/Upp`_Sculptor`_en`-us`#Upp`:`:Sculptor`:`:Translate`(const Point3D`&`)^ t
ranslation], [^topic`:`/`/Sculptor`/src`/Upp`_Sculptor`_en`-us`#Upp`:`:Sculptor`:`:Scale`(const Point3D`&`)^ s
caling], and [^topic`:`/`/Sculptor`/src`/Upp`_Sculptor`_en`-us`#Upp`:`:Sculptor`:`:Rotate`(const Point3D`&`)^ r
otation] modify the active matrix state at the top of the stack. 
This transformed state is then applied uniformly to any subsequent 
geometry [^topic`:`/`/Sculptor`/src`/Upp`_Sculptor`_en`-us`#Upp`:`:Sculptor`:`:Render`(const Model3D`&`)^ r
endered] during that pipeline cycle.&]
[s3;:2:%- 2. Core Concepts and Usage Principles&]
